WEBVTT

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.150
Yeah, the jumpsuit's in the new bubble skin fabric.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.530
Oh, it'd really suit you.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.730
What is this bubble skin?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.210
Well, it's a new kind of fabric.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.350
Well, they're saying it's as comfortable as your own skin.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:29.970
Well, it's all the rage. Everybody's...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:51.420
wearing it. God, I'm there alive. Did you hear that? Alive. Resist. Fight back. Resist.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.110
That has done it.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.280
It was much harder that time,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.220
as though the bubble skin on Sue Tye

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.150
knew somehow what happened to the one on Mike.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.650
And it had almost managed to work out a way

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.890
to resist the treatment.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.060
Aliens, I think.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.250
And the source of those bubbles.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.830
Masters are waiting.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:26.880
Who are you?

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.010
What do you want?

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:28.570
Where are you from?

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.970
You must not question the...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.090
At all! At all!

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:38.620
Andrew.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:46.190
Lord.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.520
Obey me.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.160
Obey my.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.200
Master. Master, I obey.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:06.360
Mike. Mike, no, don't let they control you.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.460
Invade. Mike.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:17.240
Invade. What happened? You seemed to take me over.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.270
I did. Maybe they've got your wavelength since you wore one.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:25.690
Obey me. Obey me.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:26.760
Look out!

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.700
It was the one bought for Elizabeth.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.900
It was attempting to control me and drain me of my powers.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.620
It would appear that they need a living host to give them their strength.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.160
If I can de-atomise them whilst they are still just jumpsuits,

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.500
they will not be able to resist.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.950
Andrew, what happened to mine and Sue Tice?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.030
No, it's all okay.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.410
We destroyed them while you were unconscious.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.600
We were stuck to you.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.890
Like they were becoming part of you.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:55.630
Ugh.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.750
Well, that accounts for those in the leg.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.130
Yeah, I think so.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:02.450
Are you...

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:03.350
Sorry.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.320
Are you OK?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:05.040
Yeah.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.480
Yeah, I think so.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.260
Thanks for dragging it off me.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.480
I was going to ask, are you OK?

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.480
Yeah, yeah, I think so.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.870
Well, the last thing I remember is John blasting us with a stun gun.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.170
Thank heaven he did.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.050
Well, where is he?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:19.970
And Elizabeth.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:26.060
Oh, they just went to find out where all the babble skins are coming from.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:28.900
Go now!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.630
Victory is ours!

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.520
What's John Elizabeth getting on?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.760
I haven't heard from them since they left.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.130
Well, let's raise them.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.350
We'd better warn them about what the bubble skins can do.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.250
Yeah, well, I think I'd better do it.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.830
They left me in charge, and when they last saw you,

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.570
you were being controlled by bubble skins.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:53.990
Okay.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.090
John, Elizabeth, are you all right?

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.640
Andrew, what shall we do about him?

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.070
You must be brought into the service of the bastards.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.990
Give me a bubble-skinned suit. I will see he wears it.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.030
He will see we wear our master's skin ourselves.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:18.990
You are right, Elizabeth.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.190
We'll cover ourselves with these.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.630
John, Elizabeth, where are you?

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.530
It's all right, Andrew.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.430
We've solved the mystery of the bubble skin suits.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.280
We're coming back to the lab.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.680
Well, that sounds like it, then.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:47.790
It's all over.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.330
I'm going to go and get dressed.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.520
You've solved the mystery of the bubble skins.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.700
What is it then?

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.640
Just a new fabric, that's all.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.740
I had one or two teething troubles with the early types,

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.620
but we've got it sorted out now.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:11.150
So we bought you a jumpsuit in the new style bubble scheme.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.280
Come on, Andrew, try it on.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.200
What's wrong with you two?

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:16.630
Those things are dangerous.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:17.790
They even tried to kill me.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:18.450
Nonsense.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.010
You've been dreaming while we were gone.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.110
Had a nightmare.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.530
Come on, Andrew, try it on.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.590
No, no, I won't.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.100
Put it on, Andrew.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.300
Oh, keep it away from me.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.740
You will eventually, so you might as well put it on now.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:28.940
No!

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.420
Hey, quick! Hey! Hey, leave him alone!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:42.180
I guess that makes us about even.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.230
It's all right, Andrew. Just as I thought.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.410
They've been taken over by the bubbles, see?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.790
Make me wear the bubble skin.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.980
They've been taken over by the bubbles like we were.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.780
or we're going to have to get them out of them.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:02.580
Aye, but how?

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.050
It gets harder every time.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:05.800
What are we going to do, Tim?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.720
Obviously, we have got to get the skins off them.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.220
Put Elizabeth on the mediprobe and I'll see.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.140
It may not be so bad

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.520
as they obviously haven't been wearing them for very long.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.530
Perhaps the skins take time to get a hold.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:20.380
What do you mean, get a hold?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.620
Well, the bubbles seem to grow

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.600
to become part of your real skin, part of you.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.040
Horrible thought.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.570
See, the suit is stuck to her skin.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.740
You tried to take it off and her skin would come with it.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:36.980
Stand back, please.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.920
It's the bubble skin that is moving, not Elizabeth.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.540
The skin has a life of its own.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.130
What is this?

00:07:59.600 --> 00:07:59.980
Bubbles.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.790
Risking isn't a stuck to Joe at all.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:07.520
What do you reckon?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:08.730
I don't know.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.550
But let's get it off in quick before it does decide to stick.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.340
Then we can wonder about why afterwards.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:18.460
They still resist, but we are strong.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.440
It is time.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.520
Masters.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.340
The time is coming.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.980
We shall soon begin the...

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:37.210
Masters, is it wise? Are you strong enough in number to show yourselves?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:42.450
We shall go out and begin the hunt.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:47.690
What hit me?

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.410
I did, with a stun gun. We quit, snail.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.640
Oh, thank goodness you did.

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.710
My bubble skin, it's gone.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.440
Yes, we were able to take yours off.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.960
That's more than we can do for...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.480
Elizabeth. Well, hers is welded to her flesh, like it was with me and Soutai.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:08.050
And mine wasn't? No, yours came off easily, like a suit of clothes.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:13.830
We know the skins developed a resistance to the method we used to remove them from Mike and Soutai.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.310
It is unlikely that method will work again.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.920
Why did my suit come off so easily, Tim? Any ideas?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:29.310
We managed to remove the double skins from Mike and Soutai by bringing into play the body's normal defence mechanism against disease and reinforcing it considerably.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:35.760
It may be that there is something about your body which makes the skins reluctant to try and become part of you.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.460
This damn cold I got, could that have anything to do with it, Tim?

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.740
What? You mean skins don't want to catch your cold?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.640
Oh, come on, let's be sensible, John.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.380
I am being sensible, Mike. What do you think, Tim?

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.020
Let's try, shall we, giving Elizabeth some of your cold virus.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.400
The worst it can do is to make her a little unwell.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:09:59.650
And it may save her.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:26.780
Take a few seconds to spread through the body.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.140
Would I see you be all right?

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.020
Tim, can't you do something?

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.190
Wait a moment.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.970
The bubble skin is reacting to the virus.

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.590
Hey, look at that.

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.010
The interference in outer space is dying down again.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:11.280
I have been able to re-establish contact with the Watchdog satellites and the Galactic Trig.

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:15.870
This is a view from one of the Watchdog satellites closest to Earth.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.720
Those are like the bubbles that attacked us back.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:20.800
Are they from outer space?

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:22.690
Yes, Andrew, they are.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.050
It's an invasion.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.350
It does seem to be an invasion, as Mike suggests.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.960
I am just beginning to pick...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.960
up police and other messages which indicate that the bubbles have come out into the open

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.460
and have started to take hostile action.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:10.010
You'll be all right in a minute. We managed to get the bubble skin suit off you.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.080
That's all right. I must have caught your cold, John.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.340
Streaming, my head's throbbing.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.640
You didn't catch it. We gave it to you by injection.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:20.000
What did you do that for?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.760
Well, it was John's idea. Well, the skin didn't stick to him like it usually does.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:26.480
So he reckoned that the skin might react badly to his cold germs.

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:28.820
So now we have the weapon to fight them.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:29.870
Thank goodness.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.120
Because they're invading. They're trying to take over the world.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:12.370
I hardly think that a few bubbles from a boutique is going to pose a drastic threat to the whole world.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.350
I wish it was that simple, Mike.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:20.120
The boutique which you and the others encountered must have been only one of thousands of ingenious outlets.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:21.920
How widespread is it, Tim?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:25.810
From the reports I have been getting, I would venture it is pretty well worldwide.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:29.600
In America and Canada, it began several hours ago.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:34.830
And here's the worrying thing, an extract from a Canadian news bulletin.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:38.470
Although there are rivers throughout Canada and the United States,

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.860
most people have now taken their bubbles and realized

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:44.160
what benefit this new joining of the two species will be to mankind.

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.180
The Prime Minister and the President of the United States

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.620
have appealed to the people of North America not to panic.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.920
I myself can vouch for the fact that a bubble is just about the best thing

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.680
that can happen to a man or woman.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:59.080
If by any chance you haven't yet found a bubble to befriend,

00:13:59.500 --> 00:13:59.980
go on.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:05.380
into the streets and look for one ask your local police to help you find one

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:13.490
he looks horrible with that thing all over him sit it's a bubble skill obviously

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.910
they feel they no longer have any need to disguise themselves as fashionable

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:25.900
clothing goodness we have the weapon fight you're cold cold common cold the

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:29.960
galactic trig has just fed me all the data they have

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:36.870
on these bubble creatures it is not very pleasant far away the tip they are known

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:42.320
as ball boys and they are a kind of parasite creature that lives on other

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:48.070
creatures yes they latch on to the native species wrap themselves around

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:53.980
them and slowly digest them that's what they're doing to us it is a process

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:57.940
which takes several months they always start with whichever is the most

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.840
advanced form of life on the planet.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.140
Then they work their way down the scale,

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:06.400
matching onto different lifeforms until they have stripped the planet bare.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.460
What must we do, Jim?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.190
John's suggestion is probably the best.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:15.960
The Bulboids have the ability to take on the same immunity to disease as their host bodies.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:20.520
But like humans, they are not immune to the common cold.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.490
Right, let's get to work then.

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:36.840
Why couldn't we jaunt straight to them?

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.390
Because Tip reports there's always somebody at the store.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:40.810
They saw his jaunt.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.120
Yeah, well, we'll walk from here.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.520
Get the cylinders and draw it back to the lab.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.520
One coming. Two security men and a bubble.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:58.580
Yeah, well, don't worry.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:15:59.820
They say it with us kids.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.360
See, we're not afraid. I think we've already been taken over.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:03.480
Oh, I hope so.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:20.520
Hey, you. You two.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:22.720
Huh?

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.360
Yes, you two, come here.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.500
We're looking for a girl.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.180
You're taking the bubble skin.

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.040
You haven't seen her, have you?

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:34.100
No, sir.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:35.990
Haven't taken the skin.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.620
How could anyone not want to take the skin?

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.380
If we see her, tell you.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.820
Good. Now on your way.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:03.160
You must accept the masters.

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.480
You must accept the masters.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:06.560
I'm ZOL!

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.770
You've got to help us.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.010
Don't be stupid.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:11.910
We're helping her by keeping out of it.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.740
We've got a more important job to do.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:14.360
Come on.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:16.910
ZOL!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:21.360
Feeling better?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:22.860
Yes.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.200
I am happy to serve the masters.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.400
Try not to make them clatter.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.380
Boy, it's horrible out there. Really horrible.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.100
They're everywhere. They've taken over almost everyone.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.040
It's just a mopping up operation from now on.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:17:59.930
We force cars.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.990
Right, then. The sooner we get into space, the better.

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:05.770
Right, well, let's get changed, then.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:10.250
Well, how early did the germs get down from space again?

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:14.670
We are magnetising them so they come along the lines of the Earth's magnetic field,

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.680
then dissipate through the air.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.420
Right, then. Let's get them into the pressure canisters.

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:27.840
There it is, the old Skylab.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:29.980
I wonder if one day they'll turn it into a...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:52.380
museum all of all for the skylight well let's get down to it look out for bubbles remember

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.180
they're quite at home in space don't remind me

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:26.660
I need you to keep a lookout. I'm sorry.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.600
Okay, don't worry about it.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:29.780
Tim!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.620
Can you coordinate us to another piece of space, John?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.620
Yes, John. I think the bubbles suspect what you're up to.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.110
There's a lot of them swarming up into space.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:51.530
Down there.

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:53.830
They must be getting steamed up.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:55.740
The bubbles do do when they're angry.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:57.470
What if they find the canisters?

00:19:58.150 --> 00:19:59.270
Well, they catch coals all the sooner.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.940
I can't see how they can unfasten them or even turn them off.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:04.860
Not unless they get control of one of us and make us go.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:08.040
Unless, folks, come on, let's jump before they score us.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:16.720
Get on!

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:21.230
All we have to do now is sit back and wait and hope that our scheme works.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:29.470
To you.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:32.450
Where's your master?

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.600
He came off and left me and I didn't do anything to offend him, honest.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:53.920
There is now the biggest and most virulent epidemic of the common cold that the world has ever seen.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.770
And how are the bald boys reacting to it, Tim?

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.100
Badly, I am glad to say.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.320
Oh, fuck!

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:21.210
Oh, master!

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:24.440
No, please, master!

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:37.960
Don't leave me.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.390
Well, they have gone.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:53.130
Oh, well done, Tim.

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.080
John, you should be congratulated.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.610
Oh, no, no, I think we all should be.

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:08.160
No, I meant for your generosity.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:10.940
Well, I'll never, ever again say that you're mean.

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:15.140
Well, after all, who else can say they've given something of theirs personally to everyone else in the world?

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:17.640
Mind you, it was a stinking cold, but it's a start, eh?

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:21.310
All things considered, I wouldn't have wished for him to give me anything else.

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:27.000
Right then, I'm ready. Buy me some new clothes.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:27.980
Oh, no.

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:29.980
No, Andrew, we like you.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.280
you just the way you are.
